Europe's teachers are high on the agenda  when EU education ministers meet in  Brussels this week The ministers want to  share information about some of the  practical methods they're using to  improve the teaching profession teacher  quality is one of the most important  factors influencing student achievement  and plays a pivotal role in the life and  employment prospects of young Europeans  The ministers will also look at ways to  improve access to higher education for  students from disadvantaged backgrounds  young people too will be the focus when  ministers responsible for youth policy  meet to debate quality employment and  its contribution to their development  well-being and social inclusion culture  ministers for their part is set to  designate arthas in denmark and pathos  in Cyprus as European capitals of  culture for 2017 valletta in Malta is  the candidate for 2018 meanwhile sports  ministers are set to name an EU  representative to the world anti-doping  agency as part of efforts to combat  doping in sport doping is becoming  increasingly sophisticated and is  threatening the integrity of sport elite  athletes are often wrong model for young  people and sport more generally brings  important social economic and health  benefits to society the head of the u.s.  Doping agency will join the ministers to  debate the role of state authorities in  fighting the use of  performance-enhancing drugs the council  will also address match-fixing and moves  to allow the European Commission to take  part in negotiations on an international  convention on the manipulation of sports  results
 

